+## D7 — Retained occurrence prototype still confounds threshold with position
+
+**Finding.** In the current proposed `minimum_occurrences` prototype, threshold
+2 always selects the last row-major component and threshold 3 selects the first.
+The constructor fixes triple copies first, unique distractors in the middle,
+and pair copies last. Exact occurrence counting is therefore unnecessary on
+the emitted support, even though the two declared thresholds are distinguishable.
+
+**Bounded execution.** `workspace/occurrence_position_probe.py` preserves the
+canonical four-neighbor component extractor and replaces only occurrence
+counting with the first/last selector. At seed `20261024`, both executable rivals
+fit all three visible demonstrations and all four normal queries. A separate
+Python-only check found the same fit on 336 pair predictions across seeds 0–23,
+both settings, and three demonstrations plus four queries per episode.
+
+**Novel-query witness and its limit.** Relocating the two unique distractors to
+the first and last scan positions makes both rivals fail. The seven exact crops,
+multiplicities `[1,1,2,3]`, four-connected separation, and all-triples-before-all-
+pairs order are preserved. This lies outside the constructor's fixed placement
+support. It is a proposed semantic generalization and a teaching/support weakness,
+not a demonstrated disagreement on a normally emitted query or inconsistent
+labels inside current support. The report records each query's origin. An
+independent-color proposed demonstration refutes the position rivals without
+reusing the held-out query.
+
+**Evidence.** The final report `checks/70c33a3391ac/position-probe-four-queries.json`
+contains 36 protected Racket executions, exact programs, visible demonstrations,
+normal queries, novel query/repair examples, output hashes and runtime identity.
+Its command receipt is `checks/70c33a3391ac/position-probe-four-queries-command.json`.
+Three focused regressions passed with
+`checks/70c33a3391ac/position-tests-final-command.json`. The earlier single-query
+probe remains provenance; use the four-query report for the current finding.
+
+**Decision.** Keep the production generator and canonical rule unchanged. Before
+native promotion of this separate prototype, vary the positions of component
+roles and include a distinguishing demonstration with unique distractors at both
+scan extremes. Add first/last selectors to the demonstration-only rival gate.
+No prototype repair, acceptance or training admission is claimed by this review.
+
+The audited production SHA-256 remains
+`c46624014b3b8b0d28cb7283e814a70858a49b8f46f47abdf91cfda5e1377a60`,
+canonical rule hash `4fc872f50360`; audited prototype SHA-256 is
+`4f08aa6813defaaa5b945c2596d3bf69b1e1cc07b2016cba65bf2aca0d4c8753`.
