+## Supported two-demo prefix: fixed-frame area shortcut
+
+A bounded review under assignment `review-e530f8a2908d6565` reproduced a new
+learnability limitation in the separate `ring_area_fill` family. Current native
+status was `accepted`, acceptance SHA-256
+`3d7504d5deaffb3c4cc0f2d4aa88f136d8f9f5a18c6ecf68419c55c4c008d14a`;
+this note does not change that status. The checked prototype SHA-256 was
+`499524a0a2ca0e3ac0615328b6cdbf0886e877470cc51aa65da8cf2b902db333`.
+
+The first two demonstration recipes both use a 13-by-14 frame, with three and
+five diagonal markers. A plausible alternative fills the rings correctly but
+selects the external object using the fixed-frame formula
+`(13 - 2*k) * (14 - 2*k)`, where `k` is marker count. Thus it can ignore the
+current frame dimensions. At seed 0 this complete Racket rival fits both
+visible demonstrations in the supported two-demo episode, yet differs on its
+first novel query in **12 cells**. The query has a 7-by-7 frame and two markers:
+the intended center area is 9, while the rival requests area 90 and leaves the
+external object unfinished. The existing third demonstration, whose frame is
+10-by-11, refutes this rival while keeping the original query novel.
+
+The returned `checks/bedcbc1cb6fb/fixed-frame-probe.py` reproduces the case.
+`fixed-frame-probe.json` retains exact sources, source hashes, protected runtime
+identity, inputs, all executed outputs, and the default-third-demo mitigation;
+`fixed-frame-probe-command.json` records the successful command. Eight protected
+Racket executions matched independent Python interpretations. Demo fitting was
+completed before query execution. No broader battery or universal hypothesis
+search was run.
+
+Suggested owner action: add this fixed-geometry competitor to the finite rival
+set, then make the two-demo construction distinguish frame dimensions as well
+as marker count and qualify the changed source. Until then, the existing
+default of three demonstrations defeats this particular rival. Production,
+parametric implementation, promotion, and acceptance records remain unchanged;
+the older production-domain audit remains a separate open question.
